"Equipment converges to configuration systematically: a per-tick system examines entities with an equipment component AND an action controller; on mismatch between resolved configuration (stance override else defaults) and in-hand equipment, it forces the registered RE-ARM action to the front of the queue IFF no matching action is already queued/active - an in-progress action finishes first. Equipment gains exactly ONE writer (the Rearm effect, via apply_resolved_armaments); menu reducers, stance adoption, and the equip/unequip acts become pure config edits. Re-arm costs a round in fiction on every path uniformly."